Q: Kotlin Type Erasure irreversible? A: <p>Indeed, type parameters of types cannot be reified, so you need to store a <code>Class</code> somewhere.</p>
<p>On the other hand, type parameters of inline functions <em>can</em> be reified. You can exploit this to allow <code>processor2</code> and <code>processor3</code> to compile, by making <code>AnnotationProcessor</code> an inline function that returns a class instance holding the lambda and a <code>Class</code>.</p>
<pre><code>class AnnotationProcessor&lt;A : Annotation&gt; (
    val process: (A) -&gt; Unit,
    val clazz: Class&lt;A&gt;
)

inline fun &lt;reified A: Annotation&gt; AnnotationProcessor(noinline process: (A) -&gt; Unit) =
    AnnotationProcessor(process, A::class.java)

// these still compile without modifications!
val processor2 = AnnotationProcessor&lt;Retention&gt; { annotation -&gt;
    println(annotation)
}

val processor3 = AnnotationProcessor { annotation: Repeatable -&gt;
    println(annotation)
}
</code></pre>

Q: Jetpack Compose Navigation: Views Disappearing when Switching Destinations A: <p>to make sure it goes back safely, i've added these:</p>
<pre class="lang-kotlin prettyprint-override"><code>                IconButton(onClick = {
                    val currentEntry = navController.currentBackStackEntry
                    val hasPrevious = navController.previousBackStackEntry != null
                    if (hasPrevious &amp;&amp; currentEntry?.lifecycle?.currentState == Lifecycle.State.RESUMED) {
                        navController.navigateUp()
                    }
                }) {
                    Icon(
                        imageVector = Icons.AutoMirrored.Filled.ArrowBack,
                        contentDescription = stringResource(R.string.back),
                        tint = MaterialTheme.colorScheme.primary
                    )
                }
</code></pre>

